---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, legalEntityIN } from '~/lib/site';
const updated = '2026-05-05';
const entity = legalEntityIN;
---

<Base
  title="Shipping & Exchange Policy · India"
  description={`Shipping and exchange policy for digital products sold by ${entity.name} on the India variant of ${site.domain}.`}
  pageType="WebPage"
  noindex={false}
>
  <section class="container-app py-20 max-w-prose-tight">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal · India</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4">Shipping &amp; Exchange Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-subtle text-fluid-sm">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-subtle text-fluid-sm">
      Applicable to purchases made on the <code class="font-mono text-xs px-1 py-0.5 rounded bg-surface-2">/in/</code> variant of {site.domain}.
    </p>

    <div class="prose mt-10 text-muted [&_h2]:text-fg [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:text-fluid-xl [&_p]:my-3 [&_strong]:text-fg [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_li]:my-1.5 [&_a]:text-brand">

      <p class="text-fluid-sm">
        This Shipping &amp; Exchange Policy is a computer-generated
        electronic record published in terms of Rule 3 of the
        Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital
        Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021 (as amended) read with the
        Information Technology Act, 2000.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Digital products only — no physical shipping</h2>
      <p>
        All products sold by <strong>{entity.name}</strong> through
        <code>{site.domain}/in/</code> are <strong>digital
        products</strong>. They consist of:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Source-code repositories, made available by adding You as a collaborator on the relevant private GitHub repository,</li>
        <li>Configuration packages and documentation included in those repositories,</li>
        <li>Access (via role assignment) to the relevant private channels of the Glitch Grow Discord server, and</li>
        <li>Lifetime entitlement to updates published by us to the same repositories.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        No physical items are shipped at any point. There are
        therefore no shipping charges, no courier or logistics
        partner involvement, no packaging materials, and no postal
        addresses required at checkout.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Delivery — what to expect after payment</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Trigger</strong>: delivery is initiated automatically as soon as Razorpay confirms payment capture. You do not need to email us or take any further action.</li>
        <li><strong>Repository access</strong>: an invitation to collaborate on the private GitHub repository for the purchased SKU is sent to the GitHub username associated with the email You used at checkout, typically within <strong>5 minutes</strong>. If You haven't provided a GitHub username at checkout, we email You at the order email asking for one within 1 working day of payment.</li>
        <li><strong>Discord access</strong>: if You have already joined our Discord server (<code>discord.gg/HBZFKMts</code>), the corresponding paid role is granted automatically. If You haven't joined yet, the welcome email contains the invite link; the paid role is granted within minutes of Your accepting it.</li>
        <li><strong>Confirmation email</strong>: a Razorpay receipt arrives immediately, and a separate "delivery confirmation" email from us follows within 15 minutes summarising the access You have been granted.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Delivery delays</h2>
      <p>
        If You have completed payment but the GitHub invitation has
        not arrived within <strong>2 working hours</strong>, please
        contact us at <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a>
        with Your Razorpay payment ID. The most common cause is a
        typo'd or unverified GitHub username at checkout, which we
        resolve manually.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are not liable for delays caused by GitHub or Discord
        platform outages, but we will keep You informed and re-issue
        invitations once the platform is healthy.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Exchange — between SKUs</h2>
      <p>
        Within <strong>14 days</strong> of purchase (7 days for the
        AI Digital Marketing Stack bundle), You may request an exchange between
        SKUs of equal or lesser monetary value, in lieu of a refund.
        We treat exchanges as a refund of the original SKU plus a
        new purchase of the replacement SKU; any difference in price
        is settled accordingly.
      </p>
      <p>
        Exchange requests are not guaranteed to be approved — they
        are at our reasonable discretion and depend on whether the
        replacement SKU is available. Where an exchange is approved,
        access to the original SKU's repository and Discord role is
        revoked simultaneously with the grant of access to the new
        SKU.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Refunds</h2>
      <p>
        Refund eligibility, windows, and processing timelines are
        covered in our separate
        <a href="/in/legal/refund">Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Address &amp; contact</h2>
      <p>
        For any question relating to delivery or exchange:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email</strong>: <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a></li>
        <li><strong>Registered office</strong>: {entity.name}, {entity.address}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
